  "notes": "All fees are list prices. Every evaluation except Fast Track and DTF is a MONTHLY subscription (auto-renews every 30 days). The site was running '90% off, grab 20 evals' at check time (e.g. 50K 1 Step $207 -> $20.70), but no code is shown publicly. Funded activation is $87/month or a one-time $177-$307 (DTF has none; Fast Track is monthly only). Note: the 1 Step landing page lists 50K/100K/250K, but the live evaluations page sells 50K/100K/150K (150K: $5,000 trailing DD); we used the evaluations page. Fast Track is two 10K variants ($57 EOD, $77 static) and both are listed as size 10000. Sim payouts are capped at $25,000 per trader; ETF may move traders to LIVE ELITE (real capital, 80/20) 'before, during, or after a payout request', and sim accounts close on conversion. Recent Trustpilot reviews (Oct 2026) complain that this live transition replaced pending sim payouts and that live accounts took a month+ to set up. ETF replies it's disclosed in its Terms. Trustpilot is 3.8 with 24% 1-star. Flagged as a risk but not excluded, since payouts are still being made (homepage Oct 2026 payout feed). The domain elitetraderfunding.com redirects to elitetraderfunding.app. Entity: Elite Trader Funding, LLC; founded 2022-02-14 by Kanwal Singh. No HQ address published. News-trading policy wasn't found on the pages checked. Overnight/weekend holding is only allowed on Diamond Hands and DTF; other plans must flatten one minute before close.",
